From 684e9504e6b95cd9c8f268155819744e8d72af94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:06:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 75/76] vgpu: speak macOS 27's protocol 237

Component: protocol negotiation and child packets (all pathways), Vulkan
device info.

A 27.2 guest asks for protocol 252. This device clamped it to 62, the
top of the 26-era ladder, and at 62 the guest's Metal plugin has
TextureDescriptor2 off: it serializes texture usage in eight bits and
refuses every texture that needs more, which includes every Liquid Glass
backdrop. The guest's kernel driver has a second ladder from 200 to 252;
237 is its lowest rung with TextureDescriptor2. A request at or above
237 now negotiates 237; anything below is clamped as before.

What 237 sends that 62 does not:
- 0x43 EXEC_INDIRECT3 and 0x45 EXEC_INDIRECT_INFO: EXEC_INDIRECT2 with
  eight-byte resource records. Both are widened to 0x37 and run on its
  rail; 0x45's command buffers hold info-segment records.
- 0x44 SET_OBJECT_LIST2: the object list named by task GVA, beside a
  second list nothing here reads. Applied through SET_OBJECT_LIST.
- Feature byte 10 (two-plane textures) on every rung of the new ladder,
  so device-info key 12 answers yes there.
- Feature byte 0x1b, which the plugin ANDs with device-info keys 23
  and 24 (tile shaders, imageblocks). The Vulkan backend has no tile
  memory, so DeviceInfoLimits gains tile_memory and the Vulkan arm
  answers 0; the Metal arm still answers 1. Below 200 the byte is off and
  the answer never mattered.

The rest of what 237 changes is in the three patches before this one.
The rung table and the opcodes were read off the 27.2 guest's kernel
driver and Metal plugin, and checked against the packets a boot sends.

Measured on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest, cold boot:
desktop, wallpaper, Dock and menus draw; "Cannot create a texture with
this usage" no longer appears in the guest log; the About window draws
as frosted glass, with its text on the first draw.

Verified:
- cargo test -p reims-vgpu --no-default-features
  --features backend-vulkan,host-window -- --test-threads=1 passes
  (2354 lib tests and the integration tests), with new tests for the
  negotiation, the rung set, the tile-memory keys and SET_OBJECT_LIST2.
- clippy reports the same 40 diagnostics as before.

Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 arms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
